<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermann von Mittnacht</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1825">1825</a>–<a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermann von Mittnacht was a Württemberg statesman who dominated the kingdom's government after German unification, serving as minister of justice from 1867 and as head of the ministry from 1876 to 1900. A moderate conservative, he worked closely with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Bismarck</a> while defending Württemberg's reserved rights, including its own army, railways and posts, within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermann-von-mittnacht.jpg" alt="Hermann von Mittnacht" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Robert Richard Brendámour · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minister_von_Mittnacht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
